      "side": 1,
      "message": "The premise doesn\u0027t hold in CI: `run-ci.sh` starts ELK and filebeat before `docker-test-host.sh`, and filebeat tails the same logs/ directory the logger writes to. With auto_delete\u003d0, every logger init runs rm -rf on all logs, deleting earlier tests\u0027 events before filebeat ships them and yanking files out from under it mid-read (the auto_delete\u003d1 path only deleted filebeat-confirmed files, so it was lossless).\n\nThis makes the host-test event stream in Elasticsearch lossy/flaky which is no bueno.\n\n\nSuggestion: gate the cleanup on an EVSSIM_ env var set by the runner, so unconditional deletion only happens when ELK is not part of the run.",
